  I just discovered a little "gotcha" that some of you
might be interested in hearing about -- it blew away about
two hours worth of ftping, unsharing, and compiling.

  Figuring that it wasn't worth doing the full installation
of 3.0 while it's so buggy, I put the source in a subdirectory
of my home-dir, and edited the makefile to install the executable
and other stuff in the same place.  Well, it turns out the
Makefile does an "rm -rf" on GAMEDIR -- in short, it wiped out
my source, object files, and everything.

  :-)

  Maybe I should have been alert to the possibility that something
like that might happen, but it might be nice to put a warning in
the installation instructions.

			 Bill


